$ chap pr merge --help
exit: 0
--- request
(none)
--- stdout
usage: chap pr merge <n> --head <sha> [--base <b>] [--repo owner/name] [--dry-run]
merge a PR when verify is green on its exact head
  -approval string
    	resume under this approval id (a-...)
  -base string
    	base branch (default "main")
  -dry-run
    	evaluate policy and preconditions only; merge nothing
  -head string
    	the PR's head sha the merge is for (required)
  -json
    	print chapd's JSON reply instead of text
  -project string
    	project slug (the orchestrator must name one; a run's is its token's) [env CHAP_PROJECT]
  -reason string
    	why (shown on the approval card, never used for authorization)
  -repo string
    	owner/name (default: from the git remote origin)
  -request
    	create the approval card for this exact op instead of running it (needs --reason)
  -wait value
    	seconds to wait for a final state, 0 to 55 (default: chapd's)
--- stderr
